{"content_hash": "cdae12a555378a8a", "version_id": 468, "article_id": 47, "level_code": "ja_n3", "lang": "ja", "level": 3, "level_label": "N3 中級", "title": "AI監視カメラのフロック、約270人を削減へ", "title_zh": "AI监控摄像头公司Flock要裁掉约270人", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "guardian_tech", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/09/flock-job-cuts", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1562739974-e15519c03d87?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8OHx8c3VydmVpbGxhbmNlJTIwc3RhcnR1cCUyMGZsb2NrfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE2NjU4NTR8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Kaspars Eglitis on Unsplash", "author": "Kaspars Eglitis", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@kasparseglitis?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/bird-on-white-cctv-camera-BCMCMuTISio?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(321, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(359, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "9651cefffeca"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-09", "word_count": 203, "reading_minutes": 0.7, "lead": "AIでナンバープレートを読むカメラを作るアメリカのスタートアップ、フロックが人員を減らします。プライバシーを心配する声が強くなっているからです。", "lead_zh": "研发AI车牌识别摄像头的美国初创公司Flock要裁员了，原因是越来越多人担心隐私问题。", "preview": "関係者によると、フロックは社員の約18％にあたる270人ほどを減らす計画です。先に希望退職を募ったあとの削減で、対象の社員は今月末に会社を去ります。会社は約1500人の社員がいますが、この計画はまだ公表していないので、関係者は名前を出していません。", "preview_zh": "据知情人士透露，Flock计划裁掉约270人，占员工总数的18%左右。这次裁员是在自愿离职计划之后进行的，被裁员工将在本月底离开公司。公司约有1500名员工，但计划还没公开，所以消息人士没有透露姓名。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 458, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/47/ja_n3.mp3", "duration": 43.038, "size_bytes": 261936, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 136, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/468.json", "paragraphs": ["関係者によると、フロックは社員の約18％にあたる270人ほどを減らす計画です。先に希望退職を募ったあとの削減で、対象の社員は今月末に会社を去ります。会社は約1500人の社員がいますが、この計画はまだ公表していないので、関係者は名前を出していません。", "フロックは2017年にアトランタで生まれ、ベンチャー投資家から9億5000万ドル以上を集めました。今年3月にはアンドリーセン・ホロウィッツが中心になって2億7500万ドルを出し、会社の価値は75億ドルになりました。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["据知情人士透露，Flock计划裁掉约270人，占员工总数的18%左右。这次裁员是在自愿离职计划之后进行的，被裁员工将在本月底离开公司。公司约有1500名员工，但计划还没公开，所以消息人士没有透露姓名。", "Flock于2017年在亚特兰大成立，从风投那里筹集了超过9.5亿美元。今年3月，安德森·霍洛维茨领投2.75亿美元，公司估值达到75亿美元。这笔钱用来建新工厂，还要进军无人机产品。"], "body": "関係者によると、フロックは社員の約18％にあたる270人ほどを減らす計画です。先に希望退職を募ったあとの削減で、対象の社員は今月末に会社を去ります。会社は約1500人の社員がいますが、この計画はまだ公表していないので、関係者は名前を出していません。\n\nフロックは2017年にアトランタで生まれ、ベンチャー投資家から9億5000万ドル以上を集めました。今年3月にはアンドリーセン・ホロウィッツが中心になって2億7500万ドルを出し、会社の価値は75億ドルになりました。", "body_zh": "据知情人士透露，Flock计划裁掉约270人，占员工总数的18%左右。这次裁员是在自愿离职计划之后进行的，被裁员工将在本月底离开公司。公司约有1500名员工，但计划还没公开，所以消息人士没有透露姓名。\n\nFlock于2017年在亚特兰大成立，从风投那里筹集了超过9.5亿美元。今年3月，安德森·霍洛维茨领投2.75亿美元，公司估值达到75亿美元。这笔钱用来建新工厂，还要进军无人机产品。", "text": "関係者によると、フロックは社員の約18％にあたる270人ほどを減らす計画です。先に希望退職を募ったあとの削減で、対象の社員は今月末に会社を去ります。会社は約1500人の社員がいますが、この計画はまだ公表していないので、関係者は名前を出していません。 フロックは2017年にアトランタで生まれ、ベンチャー投資家から9億5000万ドル以上を集めました。今年3月にはアンドリーセン・ホロウィッツが中心になって2億7500万ドルを出し、会社の価値は75億ドルになりました。", "vocab": [{"word": "削減", "pos": "noun", "zh": "削减、裁员", "note": "常和「人員」「費用」搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "関係者", "pos": "noun", "zh": "相关人士、知情者", "note": "新闻里常用来表示消息来源", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "希望退職", "pos": "noun", "zh": "自愿离职、自愿退休", "note": "公司劝员工主动辞职的制度", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "公表", "pos": "noun", "zh": "公布、公开", "note": "「公表する」是常用动词形", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "監視", "pos": "noun", "zh": "监视、监控", "note": "「監視カメラ」是监控摄像头", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "ナンバープレート", "pos": "noun", "zh": "车牌", "note": "也可说「ナンバー」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "自動で", "pos": "adv", "zh": "自动地", "note": "修饰动词，表示不用人工", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "読み取る", "pos": "verb", "zh": "读取、识别", "note": "常和机器、数据搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "反発", "pos": "noun", "zh": "反对、反弹", "note": "比「反対」语气更强", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "世論", "pos": "noun", "zh": "舆论、民意", "note": "「世論調査」是民意调查", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "賛成", "pos": "noun", "zh": "赞成", "note": "反义词是「反対」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "争点", "pos": "noun", "zh": "争议焦点", "note": "选举新闻里常用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "AI surveillance startup Flock to cut several hundred jobs amid backlash, sources say", "summary_original": "Company, which grown rapidly in recent years, has been under scrutiny as privacy concerns grow\nFlock Safety plans to shed about 18% of its employees, people with direct ⁠knowledge of the plans said on Thursday, as the maker of\nAI\n-powered\nsurveillance\ncameras and license-plate readers faces\nmounting opposition\nto its products from communities and ⁠lawmakers.\nThe people said the job ⁠cuts came after ​a voluntary buyout program and were expected to affect roughly 270 employees at Flock, a surveillance technology startup that has seen rapid growth in recent ⁠years. Employees will leave the company at the end of the month.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "AI surveillance startup Flock to cut several hundred jobs amid backlash, sources say\nCompany, which grown rapidly in recent years, has been under scrutiny as privacy concerns grow\nFlock Safety plans to shed about 18% of its employees, people with direct ⁠knowledge of the plans said on Thursday, as the maker of\nAI\n-powered\nsurveillance\ncameras and license-plate readers faces\nmounting opposition\nto its products from communities and ⁠lawmakers.\nThe people said the job ⁠cuts came after ​a voluntary buyout program and were expected to affect roughly 270 employees at Flock, a surveillance technology startup that has seen rapid growth in recent ⁠years. Employees will leave the company at the end of the month.\nSources declined to be identified as the company has yet to make the plan public.\nFlock declined ⁠to comment.\nIn September, Flock announced a voluntary separation program, asking employees to apply if they wanted to ​leave the company, as Wired reported. The ‌company has about 1,500 employees.\nFlock faces ‌\ngrowing scrutiny\nfrom regulators, lawmakers and privacy advocates, despite drawing strong investor interest among venture capitalists. A ‌recent Reuters/Ipsos poll showed Americans are divided on whether Flock cameras are a good idea. About 38% of the country supports the use of Flock cameras in their community, compared with 47% who oppose their use.\nAcross 49 states, Flock’s network of about 120,000 AI-powered cameras, affixed to streets and highways, automatically read license plates and record vehicles as they pass.\nThe company, based in Atlanta and founded in ‌2017, has raised more than $950m from venture capital investors, with its latest $275m round in March led by Andreessen Horowitz valuing the company at $7.5bn. The funds have supported a ​new US manufacturing facility and an upcoming push into drone products, according to the company.\nFlock provides cameras and software to more than 4,800 law enforcement agencies and nearly 1,000 businesses. The company says its technology helps investigate and solve crimes, but it has come under increasing scrutiny over alleged privacy violations and data-sharing practices.\nPublic backlash ⁠has grown. In September, Florida banned automated license plate readers from state highways, ​citing privacy risks tied to Flock’s ​cameras.\nHome Depot investors recently demanded reviews ​of the retailer’s partnerships with surveillance technology vendors after reports that Flock’s data was used ​in immigration enforcement.\nFlock also ‌faces legal challenges, such ​as a privacy ​lawsuit in Virginia alleging that the widespread deployment of its AI-powered cameras constitutes warrantless surveillance.\nTogether with AI datacenters, Flock cameras have emerged as a flashpoint ahead of November’s midterm elections, with candidates increasingly attacking their opponents by tying them to the technology.\nExplore more on t